From: SOAR Lab <local>
Date: 2026-11-08
Subject: worker: async dispatch inside setWorkflowExecution

setWorkflowExecution calls handleExecutionResult (decide + child
dispatch) synchronously. Since callers include the /api/v1/streams
handler, every app-side send_result POST blocked on the full dispatch
cycle, exceeding the app SDK 10s read timeout under parallel fanout -
Read timeouts, retry storms, duplicate deliveries.

State is durable in cache before this point and handleExecutionResult
recomputes from it, so dispatch can run in a goroutine. Callers never
consumed the dispatch (void function); the FINISHED path still
validates + shuts down synchronously, so the last result cannot orphan
pending children.
diff --git a/functions/onprem/worker/worker.go b/functions/onprem/worker/worker.go
index fb7b3e5..79fd7a3 100644
--- a/functions/onprem/worker/worker.go
+++ b/functions/onprem/worker/worker.go
@@ -279,7 +279,11 @@ func setWorkflowExecution(ctx context.Context, workflowExecution shuffle.Workflo
 		return err
 	}
 
-	handleExecutionResult(workflowExecution)
+	// Dispatch asynchronously: the execution state is durable in cache and
+	// decide recomputes from it. Holding callers (incl. the /api/v1/streams
+	// handler response) for the full dispatch cycle caused app-side 10s
+	// send_result timeouts and retry storms under parallel fanout.
+	go handleExecutionResult(workflowExecution)
 	validated := shuffle.ValidateFinished(ctx, -1, workflowExecution)
 	if validated {
 		shutdownData, err := json.Marshal(workflowExecution)
